 "brief": "Settlers stole olive fruit from Palestinian farmers in Beit Imrin, a village northwest of Nablus, the Ma'an news agency reported. The incident marks a recurring pattern of agricultural theft targeting Palestinian communities during harvest season in the occupied West Bank.\n\nBeit Imrin lies in an area where Palestinian farmers face regular confrontations with Israeli settlers over land access and crop harvesting. Olive cultivation remains a vital economic resource for West Bank communities, particularly during the autumn harvest period.",
